# OTOS Module — photo selection manifest
# Lists ONLY the shots we keep, and what each becomes in the guide.
# Format:  SOURCE   target.webp      (# comments + blank lines ignored)
# Convert with (any OS — needs `pip install pillow pillow-heif`):
#   python3 tools/convert_build_photos.py <staging-dir> docs/assets/build/otos/photos.manifest docs/assets/build/otos
# That holds every output under the 300 KB target in docs/assets/build/README.md.
#
# Source: the "2 - Optical Tracking Odometry Sensor Module Build" Drive folder,
# split into Construction/ (bench build, already numbered 1-16 in build order)
# and Attachment/ (fitting the finished module to the robot, labelled Part 1-3).
#
# Numbering here runs straight through the page: 01-16 ARE the Construction
# source numbers, so a photo traces back to its shot. Attachment continues at 17
# rather than restarting, so the page reads in order top to bottom. The two
# Wire_setup HEICs sit at 17-18 because they show the bus-side lead being made
# up, which has to happen before Part 1 puts the shifter in its housing.

# --- Construction — bench build (source numbers preserved) ---
Construction/1.jpg        01-otos-board-film-on.webp
Construction/2.jpg        02-otos-board-film-off.webp
Construction/3.jpg        03-sensor-in-cradle.webp
Construction/4.jpg        04-cradle-seated-in-housing.webp
Construction/5.jpg        05-housing-closed-around-sensor.webp
Construction/6.jpg        06-sensor-aperture-underside.webp
Construction/7.jpg        07-standoff-screws-inserted.webp
Construction/8.jpg        08-standoff-screws-seated.webp
Construction/9.jpg        09-shifter-and-housing-laid-out.webp
Construction/10.jpg       10-level-shifter-silkscreen.webp
Construction/11.jpg       11-lever-nut-block.webp
Construction/12.jpg       12-first-lead-landed.webp
Construction/13.jpg       13-block-with-lead.webp
Construction/14.jpg       14-four-leads-landed.webp
Construction/15.jpg       15-block-both-sides-landed.webp
Construction/16-Done.jpg  16-bench-harness-complete.webp

# --- Attachment — fitting the module to the robot ---
Attachment /Wire_setup_IMG_1485.HEIC                  17-crimp-pins-and-lead.webp
Attachment /Wire_setup_IMG_1484.HEIC                  18-bus-lead-terminated.webp
Attachment /Part 1_ 5v-_3v stepdown into 3d part.jpg  19-shifter-into-housing.webp
Attachment /Part 2_ wire management.jpg               20-wire-management.webp
